{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"OESA-2026-2170","published":"2026-05-03T11:11:09Z","modified":"2026-08-18T01:19:50.896728306Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-6245"],"summary":"sssd security update","details":"Provides a set of daemons to manage access to remote directories and authentication mechanisms. It provides an NSS and PAM interface toward the system and a pluggable back end system to connect to multiple different account sources. It is also the basis to provide client auditing and policy services for projects like FreeIPA.\r\n\r\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\nA flaw was found in the System Security Services Daemon (SSSD). The pam_passkey_child_read_data() function within the PAM passkey responder fails to properly handle raw bytes received from a pipe. Because the data is treated as a NUL-terminated C string without explicit termination, it results in an out-of-bounds read when processed by functions like snprintf(). A local attacker could potentially trigger this vulnerability by initiating a crafted passkey authentication request, causing the SSSD PAM responder to crash, resulting in a local Denial of Service (DoS).(CVE-2026-6245)","affected":[{"package":{"name":"sssd","ecosystem":"openEuler:24.03-LTS-SP1","purl":"pkg:rpm/openEuler/sssd&distro=openEuler-24.03-LTS-SP1"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"2.9.4-18.oe2403sp1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"aarch64":["libipa_hbac-2.9.4-18.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","libipa_hbac-devel-2.9.4-18.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","libsss_autofs-2.9.4-18.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","libsss_certmap-2.9.4-18.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","libsss_certmap-devel-2.9.4-18.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","libsss_idmap-2.9.4-18.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","libsss_idmap-devel-2.9.4-18.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","libsss_nss_idmap-2.9.4-18.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","libsss_nss_idmap-devel-2.9.4-18.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","libsss_sudo-2.9.4-18.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","python3-libipa_hbac-2.9.4-18.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","python3-libsss_nss_idmap-2.9.4-18.oe2403sp1.